.\" Man page for renamer. View it with:  man ./renamer.1
.TH RENAMER 1 "2026-10-31" "renamer 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
renamer \- rename TV episode files and fix the tags inside them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B renamer
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B renamer meta
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B renamer \-\-sort
.RB [ \-\-clean ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B renamer \-\-clean
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B renamer \-\-make\-names
.I FILE
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B renamer \-\-undo
|
.B \-\-reset
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B renamer lib \-\-sort
|
.B \-\-group
|
.B \-\-genre
.RI [ LIBRARY ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B renamer
renames the episode files of a TV show to
.BR Show\-Name_S01E04_Episode\-Title.mkv ,
with the episode titles from TVmaze, and can also rename the show and season folders, write
Kodi
.I .nfo
files, move junk out of the way, sort loose videos into season folders, and check and fix the
tags inside the videos (title, show, season, episode, plot and so on) for players such as VLC,
mpv, Jellyfin and Plex.
.PP
Every run first works out everything it would do and shows it as a
.BR preview ,
then asks one question.
.B Nothing is changed until you answer y.
Every change is written to an undo log as it is made, so
.B renamer \-\-undo
can reverse the run afterwards.
.PP
.I PATH
is a show folder (every season folder in it is handled) or one season folder (its parent is
taken as the show folder). A season folder that sits directly in a TV library, with other shows
next to it, is its own show folder: its undo log,
.I .nfo/
and
.I .junk/
stay inside it.
.B renamer meta
also takes a single video file.
.I .
is the current folder, and so is no
.I PATH
when other options are given:
.B renamer \-\-meta
inside a show folder handles that show.
.B renamer
on its own, or
.B renamer meta
on its own, prints a short summary of the options and changes nothing.
.PP
Renaming is the plain
.B renamer
command. Other kinds of work have their own word after it, like
.BR "renamer meta" ;
a folder that is really called
.I meta
is given as
.IR ./meta .
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show the help: one section per kind of work, as below.
.B renamer meta \-\-help
shows only the META section. A long help opens in
.BR less .
.SH RENAMING
.B renamer
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.PP
Renames each video, and the subtitles that go with it
.RI ( Show.S01E04.en.srt ,
the files in a season's
.I Subs
folder), to
.BR Show\-Name_S01E04_Episode\-Title.ext .
A file holding two episodes becomes
.BR Show\-Name_S01E01E02_Title\-1+Title\-2.mkv .
The season and episode come from the
.B SxxEyy
or
.B 1x04
in the filename, or from the season folder's name and the order of the files.
.PP
.B Changes:
file names. Folder names,
.I .nfo
files, junk and the tags inside the videos only with the options below. Videos are never
deleted; junk only when you answer
.BR DELETE .
.TP
.BI \-\-show " NAME" "\fR, \fP\-s " NAME
Use this show name and skip the show-name question.
.TP
.BI \-\-names " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-n " FILE
Take the titles from a nameInfo file instead of TVmaze. The run is then offline. See
.BR "NAMES FILE" .
.TP
.BR \-\-fix\-folders ", " \-f
Also rename the show folder
.RI ( Show\-Name_Seasons_01\-08 )
and the season folders
.RI ( Season_01_Show\-Name ,
the number first so a file browser shows it however long the name). A season the show calls
something else keeps that:
.I Book One \- Air
becomes
.IR Book_01_Air_Show\-Name ;
Volume, Chapter and Series work the same way.
.TP
.BR \-\-years ", " \-y
Put the show's years in the show folder name
.RI ( Show\-Name_2013\-present_Seasons_01\-08 ).
Season folders never get a year.
Needs
.BR \-\-fix\-folders .
.TP
.BR \-\-nfo ", " \-m
Also write Kodi
.I .nfo
files (one per episode and a
.IR tvshow.nfo )
into the hidden
.I .nfo/
folder.
.TP
.BR \-\-meta ", " \-t
Rename as usual,
.B and also
check and fix the tags inside the videos, as
.B renamer meta
does. The tags are written to the files' new names after the renames. For tags only, without
renaming, use
.BR "renamer meta" .
.TP
.BR \-\-clean ", " \-c
Also move junk (samples,
.IR .txt ,
.IR .url ,
.IR .sfv ,
screenshots, programs) to the hidden
.I .junk/
folder, keeping its path. The final question becomes
.BR [y/n/DELETE] ;
typing
.B DELETE
in capitals deletes the junk instead. On its own, with no renaming options,
.B \-\-clean
only cleans; see
.BR "CLEAN ONLY" .
.TP
.B \-\-renumber
When a filename's title matches TVmaze's title for a different episode number, use TVmaze's
number. Without it, such files keep their number and are flagged.
.TP
.B \-a
The usual full run without tags: the same as
.BR "\-\-verbose \-\-clean \-\-years \-\-fix\-folders \-\-nfo" .
.TP
.B \-\-all
The usual full run with tags: everything
.B \-a
does, plus
.BR \-\-meta .
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-v
Explain every decision (where each season, episode, title and show name came from, every
request to TVmaze) and save the output to a log file in
.IR ~/.logs/ .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-pager
Print a long preview straight to the terminal instead of opening it in
.BR less .
.SS Plain episode numbers and overall numbering
Files with only a number
.RI ( "Show \- 12" ", " Episode01.mp4 ", " "Episode 10 Doubt" ", " "[18] Title" )
are compared with TVmaze's list. The number counts the season when it fits the season, and the whole
show when it runs past the season's end or nothing says which season it is. The preview notes
.B overall episode N
when that changes the number. A number past the end of the list is left alone, as
.BR UNMATCHED .
.PP
Shows TVmaze lists by calendar year, such as Example Show, keep their overall number, as wide as the
show's total, in Wikipedia's seasons:
.IR Example\-Show_S16E0623_Title.mkv .
.PP
.B S02E13
in a 12\-episode season counts on from season 1, so it's S02E01. A release that splits its seasons
differently from TVmaze but adds up to the same total is counted through, and shown as
.BR RENUMBERED .
.SS Season folder names
With
.BR \-\-fix\-folders ,
a season with a name of its own from TVmaze or Wikipedia takes it:
.IR Season_16_Season\-Name .
Otherwise it's
.IR Season_01_Show\-Name .
A folder with
.B Dub
or
.B English Dub
in its name, or most of its files, gets
.B _Dub
at the end of the show folder name.
.SS How the show name is found
With
.BR \-\-show ,
that name is used. Otherwise the show folder's name is cleaned (anything from a year, a
.BR ( ,
a season code or a release tag such as
.B 1080p
on is dropped) and searched for on TVmaze, and TVmaze's own name for the show goes into the
filenames.
.PP
When the filenames name a different show than the folder does (a show kept in a folder called
.IR Scifi ,
with files called
.IR Example.Show\-s01e01.mkv ),
renamer asks which to search for, with the filenames' name first:
.PP
.nf
.RS
The folder and the files name different shows:
  1) Example Show  (from 173 filenames)
  2) Scifi          (the show folder name)
Search TVmaze for [1], or type a name:
.RE
.fi
.PP
When TVmaze has several shows of the same name, renamer picks by the year in the folder or file names,
then the episode titles, then the episode numbers. When TVmaze still has several matching shows,
renamer lists them with their years. Type the number
of the right one,
.B 0
or another name to search again, or press Enter for the first. When TVmaze has none, renamer
offers Wikipedia's suggestion for the name, then asks you to type one.
.SH META (TAGS ONLY)
.B renamer meta
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.PP
Reads the tags inside the videos with
.B ffprobe
(and
.B mkvmerge
for MKV), compares them with TVmaze, and fixes them: title, show, season, episode, air date,
plot, genre, network, rating, IMDb/TVDB/TVmaze IDs, the language of audio and subtitle tracks
that have none, and a single default audio track. Other tags in the file are kept. A value
TVmaze doesn't have is left as it is, never removed.
.PP
MKV files are changed in place with
.BR mkvpropedit ,
in seconds. MP4 and AVI files are copied by
.B ffmpeg
with the new tags (no re-encoding); the copy is checked (same streams, same length) before it
replaces the original. AVI only holds a title, genre, date and comment.
.PP
.B Changes:
only the tags inside the videos. Never renames or moves anything.
.B \-\-view
and
.B \-\-compare
change nothing at all.
.TP
.B \-\-view
List the tags already in the videos, file by file, in a readable form: the standard tags, any
other tags, and the audio and subtitle tracks with their language and default flag. Needs no
internet, asks nothing, writes no undo log.
.TP
.B \-\-compare
List each tag beside what TVmaze has, marked
.BR same ,
.B different
(old \(-> TVmaze's value) or
.BR missing ,
and the track fixes renamer would make. Ends with how many videos match. Changes nothing.
Implies
.BR \-\-view .
.TP
.BI \-\-show " NAME" "\fR, \fP\-s " NAME
Use this show name and skip the show-name question.
.TP
.BI \-\-names " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-n " FILE
Take the titles from a nameInfo file instead of TVmaze (offline). Only the title, show,
season and episode tags are then set.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-v
Show every tag's old and new value and save the output to
.IR ~/.logs/ .
.TP
.BR \-\-undo ", " \-u
Reverse the most recent run (the same as
.BR "renamer \-\-undo" ).
.TP
.BR \-\-reset ", " \-r
Reverse the most recent run completely (the same as
.BR "renamer \-\-reset" ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-pager
Print a long preview straight to the terminal.
.SH SORT
.B renamer \-\-sort
.RB [ \-\-clean ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.PP
Gathers a show's videos from loose files, release folders and wrongly named folders into
.I Season_NN
folders, with their subtitles. When there are several copies of one episode, the best one
stays (higher resolution, then the bigger file) and the others go to the hidden
.I .duplicates/
folder. A video whose filename names another show goes to
.I ../unsorted/
next to the show folder. Run
.B renamer
again afterwards to rename the files.
.PP
.B Changes:
where the files are. Renames nothing.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort ", " \-o
Sort mode. Can only be combined with
.B \-\-clean
and
.BR \-\-verbose .
.TP
.BR \-\-clean ", " \-c
Also move junk to
.I .junk/
and remove the folders left empty.
.SH CLEAN ONLY
.B renamer \-\-clean
.RI [ PATH ]
.PP
Only cleans: junk, samples and screenshots go to
.IR .junk/ ,
and folders left completely empty are removed. Always with the full
.B \-\-verbose
output and log.
.PP
.B Changes:
moves junk to
.I .junk/
(or deletes it when you answer
.BR DELETE )
and removes empty folders. Renames nothing.
.SH NAMES FILE
.B renamer \-\-make\-names
.I FILE
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B renamer \-\-names
.I FILE
.RI [ PATH ]
.PP
For shows TVmaze numbers differently from your files, or to work offline. A nameInfo file has
a line per season
.RB ( S01 )
followed by one title per video file, in order. Two episodes in one file are joined with
.BR " + " .
Lines starting with
.B #
are comments.
.TP
.BI \-\-make\-names " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-g " FILE
Write TVmaze's titles for the show to
.IR FILE ,
to edit and use with
.BR \-\-names .
Renames nothing; refuses to overwrite an existing file.
.TP
.BI \-\-names " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-n " FILE
Rename from that file, without going online. Missing titles are asked for.
.SH UNDO AND RESET
.B renamer \-\-undo
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B renamer \-\-reset
.RI [ PATH ]
.PP
Reverse the most recent run in the show folder, from its undo log, after the same preview and
question: renames and folder renames go back, junk comes back out of
.IR .junk/ ,
the
.I .nfo
files the run created are deleted (unless you edited them since), and the tags inside the
videos are put back. Each run can be reversed once; running it again steps back one more run.
.TP
.BR \-\-undo ", " \-u
Old
.I .nfo
files the run archived stay in
.IR .nfo/.nfo\-old/ .
.TP
.BR \-\-reset ", " \-r
Everything goes back exactly as it was, old
.I .nfo
files included.
.SH LIBRARY: GATHERING SHOWS
.B renamer lib \-\-sort
.RB [ \-\-clean ]
.RI [ LIBRARY ]
.PP
Tidies a library folder whose shows are in pieces. Each piece is matched to its TVmaze show
(by renamer's own ID in
.I tvshow.nfo
or MKV tags, else by name), and the pieces of one show gather in one show folder:
.IP \(bu 2
several folders of the same show
.RI ( "Example Show" ,
.IR Example\-Show_1997\-present_Seasons_01\-26 ,
.IR "Example Show Season 27 and 28" );
.IP \(bu 2
lone season folders
.RI ( "Example Show (2005) Season 1 S01" ", " "\[u2026] Season 2 S02" );
.IP \(bu 2
loose episode files at the top of the library
.RI ( Example.Show.S29E01\[u2026]mkv );
.IP \(bu 2
season folders with no show name
.RI ( "SEASON 02" ),
matched by their episode titles against the library's other shows.
.PP
Shows are told apart by their TVmaze ID, never by name alone, so spin-offs
.RI ( "Example Show: Spin-Off" )
stay separate. The pieces go into the folder already inside a genre folder, else the one in
renamer's own format, else the one with the most episodes; when there's no show folder yet, a
new one named by TVmaze
.RI ( Example\-Show/ ).
Download sites' names
.RI ( www.example-site.org \- )
and extras like
.I +Specials
are left out of the show name.
.PP
A folder around the seasons with a generic name
.RI ( Series/ ", " Seasons/ ", " Episodes/ ", " Shows/ ", " TV/ ", " "TV Series/" ", " Complete/ )
is removed, its contents moved up into the show folder.
.PP
Movies found in the TV library go to a folder called
.I Movies
in
.IR ../ ,
.I ../../
or
.I ../../../
(for an animated library,
.I Movies(Animated)
first), else to a hidden
.I .movies/
in the library. That includes movies beside a show's seasons: a folder or video with a year in
its name and no episode numbers, unless a show has more than three of those, which are taken as
its specials. A movies folder on another disk is a
.BR CONFLICT .
.PP
Then, in a second preview and question, the episodes inside each show that got new pieces go
into season folders, as
.B renamer \-\-sort
does. When an episode has several copies, the one whose name looks like the show's own files (the
same release) is kept, else the best quality; the others go to
.IR .duplicates/ .
.PP
Left alone, and listed: bundles of several shows (numbered parts:
.IR "1a. Example Show \- Part One" ),
any show with a download still in progress
.RI ( .!qb ),
and qBittorrent's hidden
.I .parts
files. Matches renamer isn't sure about are listed after the preview to change or leave. A
read\-only library gets the preview only.
.B renamer lib \-\-undo
reverses the last step; run it twice for both.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort ", " \-s
Gather each show's pieces into one show folder and sort its episodes into season folders.
.TP
.BR \-\-clean ", " \-c
With
.BR \-\-sort :
also move junk to
.I .junk/
and remove the folders left empty.
.PP
A folder holding two shows of one name is split by the year in the names, episode titles and episode
numbers:
.IR "Example 1/2/" " becomes " Example\-½_1989/ " and " Example\-½_2024/ .
What can't be told apart stays where it is. A dub stays apart from the show's other copies, in a
.I _Dub
folder. A folder of movies with years in their names moves to the movies library whole.
.SH LIBRARY: KEEPING COPIES TOGETHER
.B renamer lib \-\-group
.RI [ LIBRARY ]
.PP
For a library holding several copies of a show, whole or partial, that you want to keep apart.
Each show with two or more copies gets one folder, named by TVmaze with no years
.RI ( Example\-Show/ ),
and each release moves into it whole, under its own name. Nothing inside a release changes:
nothing is merged, renamed or deleted, and movies and
.I Series/
folders stay where they are.
.PP
Loose episode files at the top of the library go in a
.I loose\-episodes/
folder inside the show's folder, with their subtitles. A copy that already has the new folder's
name ends up inside it
.RI ( Example-Show/Example-Show/ ).
A show with one copy stays where it is, and shows are told apart by their TVmaze ID, so spin\-offs
get folders of their own. Bundles of several shows, movies and any show still downloading
.RI ( .!qb )
are left alone. Matches renamer isn't sure about are listed after the preview to change or leave.
.PP
The folder holds a small hidden file,
.IR .renamer\-group ,
with the show's TVmaze ID. Because of it, a later
.B \-\-group
adds new copies to the folder,
.B \-\-sort
leaves it alone,
.B \-\-genre
moves it as one show, and plain
.B renamer
asks for one of the releases inside it.
.PP
.B Changes:
only where whole releases and loose episodes are. A torrent still seeding from a release loses
track of its files unless you move it in qBittorrent instead.
.B renamer lib \-\-undo
reverses the run.
.TP
.BR \-\-group ", " \-G
Keep each show's copies together in one folder.
.SH LIBRARY: GENRE FOLDERS
.B renamer lib \-\-genre
.RI [ LIBRARY ]
.br
.B renamer lib \-\-undo
.RI [ LIBRARY ]
.PP
Works on a whole library folder, such as
.IR TV/ ,
.I TV (Animated)/
or
.IR Movies/ .
Each show folder, movie folder or loose movie file at its top moves, as a whole, into a genre
folder in the library:
.I TV/Example Show/
becomes
.IR TV/Comedy/Example Show/ .
Nothing inside it changes. Folders that already are genre folders (a genre's name, its folder
name in the config, or an alias, so
.I Scifi/
counts as Science-Fiction), and everything already in them, stay where they are.
.PP
A folder with season folders or episode videos is a show: renamer finds it on TVmaze (by the
TVmaze ID in renamer's own
.I tvshow.nfo
or MKV tags when there is one, else by name, with Wikipedia's suggestion when TVmaze finds
nothing) and takes TVmaze's genres. Anything else with videos is a movie: renamer finds it on
Wikidata by title and year (or through Wikipedia's search) and takes its genres. Either way, the
first sentence of the Wikipedia article ("\[u2026]an American science fiction drama television
series") decides which genre is the main one. When it names exactly one of the genres, or there
is only one, renamer is sure; otherwise it guesses (the first one Wikipedia names, or the
config's order) and marks the row
.BR GUESS .
.PP
After the preview, the guesses are listed with their genres and why renamer isn't sure.
Type their numbers (or
.BR all )
to change them: pick a folder from the list, type a folder name,
.B 0
to leave it where it is, or
.B s
to search TVmaze for a different show. Then the usual question.
.PP
.B Changes:
only where the show and movie folders are, and new genre folders. A show still downloading
.RI ( .!qb )
or whose name is already in its genre folder is a
.BR CONFLICT .
A genre folder that holds a show's season folders directly (no show folder) is offered a show
folder first:
.IR Scifi/Example\-Show/ .
.B renamer lib \-\-undo
moves everything back and removes genre folders it made, if they're empty.
.PP
Lookups are cached for 30 days, so a second run is quick. TVmaze is asked at most 20 times in
10 seconds, Wikipedia and Wikidata once a second.
.TP
.BR \-\-genre ", " \-g
Sort into genre folders.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-v
Explain every decision and save the output to
.IR ~/.logs/ .
.TP
.BR \-\-undo ", " \-u
Reverse the most recent lib run.
.TP
.BR \-\-reset ", " \-r
Reverse the most recent lib run completely.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-pager
Print a long preview straight to the terminal.
.SH QUESTIONS RENAMER MAY ASK
Some problems renamer can fix there and then, after a yes. In each case you still see the usual
preview and question before anything changes.
.TP
.B Move them up into the show folder and remove Series/?
The seasons are one folder further down, in a folder with a generic name, as in
.IR Show.S01\-S13/Series/Season\ 1/ .
Giving the release or its
.I Series/
folder does the same thing, and the show's name comes from the release. No stops the run with
nothing changed.
.TP
.B Move it to /mnt/media/Movies/?
A folder or video beside the seasons has a year in its name and no episode numbers, so it looks
like a movie. It goes where
.B renamer lib \-\-sort
would put it; its featurettes go with it. No leaves it where it is, and it's listed as ignored.
Moving the seasons up and moving movies out are one run in the undo log, and the rename is
another.
.TP
.B Sort them into season folders first?
Videos are in release folders inside the show folder, loose next to season folders, or the
folder is one season sitting directly in the library. Yes runs
.B renamer \-\-sort
on it (with its own preview and question), then looks at the folder again and carries on with
the rename. The sort and the rename are two runs in the undo log.
.B renamer meta
never moves files, so it only warns.
.TP
.B Use TVmaze's numbers for these?
Filenames whose titles belong to another TVmaze episode number. Yes does what
.B \-\-renumber
does.
.TP
.B Write TVmaze's titles to a file, open it in your editor, and rename from it?
TVmaze numbers the show differently from the files (it counts segments, or a season is longer
or shorter). Yes writes the titles to
.IR ~/.local/share/renamer/names/<Show>.txt ,
opens it in
.B $VISUAL
or
.B $EDITOR
(or nano, or vi), and renames from it once you save and close it, as
.B \-\-names
would. The next run on the show offers the same file again, with your edits.
.TP
.B Try them again now?
Files that were in use (playing over SMB) and skipped. Yes tries them again, in the same run.
.SH THE PREVIEW
Each file is listed with a status, the old name, and the new name on the line below. A long
preview opens in
.B less
(or
.BR $PAGER );
press
.B q
and only the
.B Needs a look
list stays on screen, above the question. Runs of three or more files in a folder that are
already correct are shown as one line
.RI ( "SKIP  Season 3/ (16 videos)" );
.B \-\-verbose
lists each one. Tag changes show their values: the ones every file shares (show, genre,
network, IDs) once, under
.BR "Tags for every file" ,
and each file's own (title, episode, air date, rating, plot) under it, with the old value when
one changes.
.TP
.B OK
will be renamed (or is fine).
.TP
.B SKIP
already correct; nothing to do.
.TP
.B TAG
its tags will be updated
.RB ( "renamer meta" ", " \-\-meta ).
.TP
.B WARN
will be changed, but something needs checking (a title that doesn't match TVmaze, a file
changed in the last two minutes, tracks with no language).
.TP
.B CONFLICT
can't be changed (the new name exists, two files claim the same episode, a tool is missing);
left alone.
.TP
.BR UNMATCHED ", " LOOSE ", " IGNORED
no season or episode found; a video loose in the show folder; a folder that isn't a season
folder. All left alone.
.TP
.BR DUPLICATE ", " RENUMBERED ", " ARCHIVE ", " JUNK ", " CREATE
another copy of an episode; given TVmaze's number
.RB ( \-\-renumber );
an old
.I .nfo
moving to
.IR .nfo/.nfo\-old/ ;
junk moving to
.IR .junk/ ;
a new
.I .nfo
file.
.PP
The question at the end counts what will happen, for example
.BR "Rename 122 files, update the tags in 122 videos? [y/N]" .
Enter, or anything but
.BR y ,
changes nothing. Ctrl\-C at the question also changes nothing.
.SH SAFETY
.IP \(bu 2
Nothing is changed before you answer
.BR y .
An existing file is never overwritten; a video is never deleted.
.IP \(bu 2
An unfinished download
.RI ( .!qb ", " .!ut )
anywhere in the show stops the run before anything else.
.IP \(bu 2
A file that is in use (playing over SMB) is asked about: retry, skip it, or stop.
.IP \(bu 2
Each change is written to the undo log as it is made, so a run stopped halfway can still be
undone.
.IP \(bu 2
Run renamer as your normal user, not with sudo, so its files aren't owned by root.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B renamer \-\-all "/mnt/media/TV/Example Show"
First run on a new show: names, folders with years,
.I .nfo
files, junk and tags.
.TP
.B renamer .
Rename the show in the current folder, nothing else.
.TP
.B renamer \-\-fix\-folders \-\-years
Rename the files and folders of the show in the current folder.
.TP
.B renamer meta .
Fix only the tags inside the videos; rename nothing.
.TP
.B renamer meta \-\-view Season_02
Look at the tags of one season without changing them.
.TP
.B renamer meta \-\-compare
See which tags differ from TVmaze, without changing them.
.TP
.B renamer \-\-sort \-\-clean
Gather loose videos into season folders and tidy up; then run
.B renamer
to rename them.
.TP
.B renamer \-\-show """Example Show""" \-\-meta
Rename and tag, naming the show yourself.
.TP
.B renamer \-\-make\-names names.txt
Write TVmaze's titles to a file to correct by hand, then
.B renamer \-\-names names.txt
renames from it.
.TP
.B renamer \-\-undo
Reverse the last run.
.TP
.B renamer lib \-\-sort /mnt/media/TV
Gather each show in a TV library into one show folder.
.TP
.B renamer lib \-\-group /mnt/media/TV
Or keep the copies of each show apart, in one folder.
.TP
.B renamer lib \-\-genre /mnt/media/TV
Then sort the shows into genre folders.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .rename_undo.json
The undo log, in the show folder.
.TP
.IR .nfo/ ", " .nfo/.nfo\-old/
New Kodi
.I .nfo
files, and the old ones moved out of the way.
.TP
.IR .junk/ ", " .duplicates/ ", " ../unsorted/
Junk, worse copies of an episode, and other shows' videos, moved out of the way.
.TP
.I ~/.logs/renamer_<Show>_<date>_<time>.log
The log of a
.B \-\-verbose
run.
.B _undo ,
.B _reset ,
.B _meta ,
.B _view ,
.B _compare ,
.B _sort ,
.B _clean
and
.B _names
are added for those runs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/renamer/genres.conf
Which genre folder each genre goes to, their priority, and other words for each genre
(written with defaults on the first
.B renamer lib
run).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/renamer/lib\-lookups.json
What
.B renamer lib
found for each show and movie, kept 30 days.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/renamer/names/
Titles files written for the editor, one per show.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
when the run finished or you answered no;
.B 1
when it stopped with an error, or nothing could be undone;
.B 130
when stopped with Ctrl\-C.
